\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {(a)} Held-out Cohen's $d$ between a selected set and a random set of equal size. Every rule preserving the allocation's \emph  {concentration} reproduces the separation --- including permuting the uncertainty scores across clusters, and ignoring them entirely; only destroying concentration collapses it. Bars are means over four cells, whiskers the range. \textbf  {(b)} Trained $S_\alpha $ for the three arms holding concentration \emph  {exactly} fixed while varying only the signal's direction; points are seeds, rules are arm means, the band is the frozen $\pm 2\hat  {\sigma }$ bar. \emph  {Source:} \texttt  {c1\_attribution.csv} (\texttt  {EXP C1} \#4); \texttt  {out/t2/abc\_metrics.csv} (\texttt  {EXP T2} \#3).}}{6}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:thesis}{{1}{6}{\textbf {(a)} Held-out Cohen's $d$ between a selected set and a random set of equal size. Every rule preserving the allocation's \emph {concentration} reproduces the separation --- including permuting the uncertainty scores across clusters, and ignoring them entirely; only destroying concentration collapses it. Bars are means over four cells, whiskers the range. \textbf {(b)} Trained $S_\alpha $ for the three arms holding concentration \emph {exactly} fixed while varying only the signal's direction; points are seeds, rules are arm means, the band is the frozen $\pm 2\hat {\sigma }$ bar. \emph {Source:} \texttt {c1\_attribution.csv} (\texttt {EXP C1} \#4); \texttt {out/t2/abc\_metrics.csv} (\texttt {EXP T2} \#3)}{figure.1}{}}
